{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Naphtali is a hind let loose.</b> In the manner of a gift, and the recipient of the gift gives אמרי שפר (fair words). And some say that hind is an allusion to Deborah, who gives אמרי שפר — an allusion to the song of Barak with her; and he said Naphtali on account of his inheritance:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:31.149650321Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}